l pieces stay outside the outline\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:594:    and whose union bitmap is LR-symmetric. These \"frame\" pieces outline the assembled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:596:    preserving their relative positions from the output, so the rectangular outline is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:603:  optional_anchors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:654:#       - Four corner singletons are intentionally present as anchors. They stay on the border, which preserves\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:691:#     - Only three structural layers are visible in the output: corner anchors, the symmetric frame, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:866:    - Use the grouped frame cells plus any corner/edge hints to anchor the rectangle, then pack all pieces so the result\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:1177:#     frame cells still appear in-place as a recognizable LR-symmetric outline inside the input;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:1178:#     they are the stable anchor. The freely scattered fill pieces are now sometimes rotated by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:1194:#     - input-orientation anchor heuristics (horizontal bars / vertical lines) are unsafe now,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:1199:#     - frame cells are pasted as one in-place outline and never overlap scattered pieces.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:1210:#     this keeps the outline readable and the changed rule local to the fragments the user handles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:1274:    In the rotation variant we intentionally avoid input-pose-dependent anchor inference:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:1462:    - One in-place LR-symmetric frame group already shows the output rectangle's outline.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:2083:    Key insight: Left-right symmetry plus the no-same-color-touching constraint make the assembly unique; corner/edge markers anchor it when present.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:2422:#       - Four corner singletons are intentionally present as anchors. They stay on the border, which preserves\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:2459:#     - Only three structural layers are visible in the output: corner anchors, the symmetric frame, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:2634:    - Use the grouped frame cells plus any corner/edge hints to anchor the rectangle, then pack all pieces so the result\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:2691:#     frame cells still appear in-place as a recognizable LR-symmetric outline inside the input;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:2692:#     they are the stable anchor. The freely scattered fill pieces are now sometimes rotated by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:2708:#     - input-orientation anchor heuristics (horizontal bars / vertical lines) are unsafe now,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:2713:#     - frame cells are pasted as one in-place outline and never overlap scattered pieces.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:2724:#     this keeps the outline readable and the changed rule local to the fragments the user handles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/_logs/combo_35.log:2788:    In the rotation variant we intentionally avoid input-pose-dependent anchor inference:\n/home/lixin