inal matching used `anchors_by_color[color]`; this silently breaks once one color may\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:51:#     appear on multiple anchors. The key must change to `(color, direction)`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:57:#     treated as anchors without ambiguity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:61:#   - The neutral direction-indicator color repeats across all anchors, so humans can notice that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:66:#   - Direction pixels live only inside anchor motifs; sprite connectors are single-pixel protrusions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:67:#     This avoids multi-layer overlaps and keeps anchors visually distinct from sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:82:    Slide interior sprites so their connector pixels dock onto matching directional border anchors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:87:    - Border anchors are isolated 2-pixel motifs: a border connector pixel plus an adjacent direction pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:90:    - Match each sprite to the anchor sharing both connector color and connector direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:91:    - Left/right-facing anchors make the sprite slide horizontally so connector column = anchor column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:92:    - Up/down-facing anchors make the sprite slide vertically so connector row = anchor row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:94:    Key insight: The extra pixel attached to each border anchor encodes a facing, so the correct pairing is determined by the connector signature (color + direction), not by color alone.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D1/2/code.py:158:    anchors_by_sig: dict[tuple[int, str], tuple[int, int]] = {}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/c