econd):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:293:    anchor_pair = random.choice(pairs)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:299:    legend_colors = _assign_legend_colors(pts, anchor_pair, palette)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:320:    # Build input: keep only the 2 anchor blocks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:322:    keep = {anchor_pair, (anchor_pair[0], anchor_pair[1] + 1)}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:367:    role: anchor the scale/offset mapping from legend to main grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:672:def _assign_legend_colors(pts, anchor_pair, palette):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:673:    \"\"\"Assign colors to legend pts via backtracking, ensuring unique anchor-pair identification.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:675:    first = anchor_pair\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:676:    second = (anchor_pair[0], anchor_pair[1] + 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:685:    anchor_colors = (a, b)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:692:            if (colors[left], col) == anchor_colors and (left, pos) != (first, second):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:696:            if (col, colors[right]) == anchor_colors and (pos, right) != (first, second):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1004:    Replicate a motif across quadrants with scaling and reflection keyed to red anchor blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1008:    - Each quadrant contains a red (2) square anchor block of varying size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1009:    - The top-left quadrant also has a colored motif attached to its red anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1015:    - Align the scaled/reflected motif so its red region overlaps the target anchor, then stamp non-bg pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1026:    # Find red anchor blocks (color 2) in each quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1028:    assert red, \"grid must contain red (color 2) anchor blocks\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1031:    anchors: dict[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int, int]] = {}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1041:        assert key not in anchors, \"each quadrant must contain exactly one red anchor block\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1042:        anchors[key] = (int(r0), int(c0), int(size))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1044:    assert (0, 0) in anchors, \"top-left quadrant must contain a red anchor block\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1045:    sr0, sc0, sL = anchors[(0, 0)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1046:    assert sL > 0, \"top-left red anchor must have positive size\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1049:    # in the TL quadrant that contains the TL red anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1074:    # For each quadrant anchor, paste a scaled/reflected version of the patch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1075:    for (qb, qr), (tr0, tc0, tL) in anchors.items():\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1095:        assert rr_red.size > 0, \"scaled source patch must contain red anchor pixels\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1120:RED = 2                 # anchor color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1131:SOURCE_ANCHOR_SIZE = 2                  # TL anchor is always 2x2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1142:# --- Target anchor parameters ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1143:TARGET_SIZE_RANGE = (1, 4)              # anchor size range for non-TL quadrants\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1158:    \"\"\"Reflect and scale the source patch for a given quadrant and target anchor size.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1216:    freeform method grows directly at pixel resolution with a 2x2 red anchor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1243:Implement the D1 anchor-scaling variant, then validate solver/generator behavior and non-degeneration against the original solver.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1244:  ✓ Design the anchor-based variant and map original assumptions to required code changes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1269:+#    - Exactly one legend pixel uses a unique anchor color. The main area contains exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1271:+#    - The anchor pixel at logical legend coordinate (ar, ac) maps to the top-left corner of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1272:+#      anchor block. The anchor block side length N is the scaling factor. Every legend pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1275:+#      where (base_r, base_c) is recovered from the anchor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1276:+#          base_r = anchor_block_r0 - ar * N\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1277:+#          base_c = anchor_block_c0 - ac * N\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1282:+#      N=3 and base=(5,9); then every legend dot expands with step 3 from that anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1284:+#      Blocks are packed on an N-scaled lattice whose pitch equals the anchor block size itself.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1287:+#    - Using only the anchor block would be too easy if the enlarged output lost local structure,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1290:+#    - The anchor color is unique in the legend and absent from every other enlarged input block\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1291:+#      because the input contains only the anchor block. This removes ambiguity without adding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1294:+#      with a unique anchor color needs at least two additional colors to avoid flat monochrome\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1299:+#      blocks. That fails here because only the anchor block is shown.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1301:+#      shared step already known. Here offset must come directly from the unique anchor match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1303:+#      same size. In this variant the anchor block itself is the scale carrier, so solver logic\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1304:+#      should bind to the anchor match rather than to spacing statistics.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1313:+#    - Across examples the anchor location changes inside the legend, and N varies from 2 to 4.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1315:+#      anchor block size determines the enlargement factor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1325:+#    - The only special color behavior is visible uniqueness of the anchor color, which is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1334:+# - Solver assumes the anchor block size is the intended scale for every legend pixel. Generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1370:+    Complete a scaled block mosaic from a top-left legend using a unique anchor match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1375:+    - Main area: exactly one visible square block shares a unique color with one legend pixel; it is the anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1379:+    - Use that anchor block's side length as the scale factor, and align the anchor pixel to the anchor block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1382:+    Key insight: Unlike the original task, scale does not come from the spacing between visible blocks; it is encoded directly by the anchor block's size, and the anchor color fixes the offset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1419:+    anchor_matches: list[tuple[int, int, int, int, int, int]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1428:+        anchor_matches.append((int(col), int(rr), int(cc), int(br0), int(bc0), int(block_size)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1430:+    assert len(anchor_matches) == 1, \"grid must contain exactly one unique legend-to-block anchor match\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1431:+    _anchor_col, ar, ac, abr, abc, block_size = anchor_matches[0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1432:+    assert block_size >= 2, \"anchor block must be at least 2x2\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1516:+def _assign_legend_colors(pts, anchor_pt, palette):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1519:+    - anchor color is unique,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1521:+    - every non-anchor palette color appears at least once,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1525:+    anchor_color = random.choice(palette)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c4d067a0/_logs/D1_alt5.log:1